#: src/introduction.md:32
msgid "A note on output"
msgstr "En bemærkning om output"

#: src/introduction.md:34
msgid ""
"goat is built to be both a pleasure to use _and_ safe to script. Friendly "
"touches — a 🐐 when everything's green, a hint about your next step — only "
"ever appear on an interactive terminal. Pipe goat into a script or ask for "
"`--json` and you get clean, stable, machine-readable output with nothing "
"decorative in the way. Set `GOAT_NO_FUN=1` and even the interactive "
"flourishes go quiet."
msgstr ""
"goat er bygget til at være både en fornøjelse at bruge _og_ sikkert at "
"scripte. Venlige detaljer — en 🐐 når alt er grønt, et hint om dit næste "
"skridt — vises kun nogensinde på en interaktiv terminal. Send goat gennem en "
"pipe til et script eller bed om `--json`, og du får rent, stabilt, "
"maskinlæsbart output uden noget dekorativt i vejen. Sæt `GOAT_NO_FUN=1`, og "
"selv de interaktive detaljer bliver stille."

#: src/getting-started.md:3
msgid ""
"You don't need a profile, a bundle, or a network to start. goat ships with a "
"sandbox so you can learn by doing, safely."
msgstr ""
"Du behøver ikke en profil, et bundle eller et netværk for at starte. goat "
"leveres med en sandbox, så du kan lære ved at gøre, sikkert."

#: src/getting-started.md:5
msgid "1. Say hello"
msgstr "1. Sig hej"

#: src/getting-started.md:11
msgid ""
"```text\n"
"◇ SANDBOX — simulated fabric, no real mesh. Run `goat init` to attach a real "
"env.\n"
"goat hello — saying `lo` to the fabric as `default` on topic `hello/"
"default`\n"
"  [t+  42ms] portal     accepted topic `hello/default` (simulated)\n"
"  [t+  74ms] fabric     routed `lo` to `hello/default` over the WireGuard "
"P2P path (simulated)\n"
"  [t+ 101ms] subscriber your subscriber received `lo` — round-trip complete "
"(simulated)\n"
"  └─ `lo`: the first message ever sent over a network (ARPANET, 29 Oct 1969) "
"— they typed \"LOGIN\" and the link crashed after two letters.\n"
"round-trip complete.\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```text\n"
"◇ SANDBOX — simuleret fabric, intet rigtigt mesh. Kør `goat init` for at "
"tilknytte et rigtigt env.\n"
"goat hello — siger `lo` til fabric som `default` på topic `hello/default`\n"
"  [t+  42ms] portal     accepterede topic `hello/default` (simuleret)\n"
"  [t+  74ms] fabric     routede `lo` til `hello/default` over WireGuard P2P-"
"stien (simuleret)\n"
"  [t+ 101ms] subscriber din subscriber modtog `lo` — tur-retur fuldført "
"(simuleret)\n"
"  └─ `lo`: den første besked, der nogensinde er sendt over et netværk "
"(ARPANET, 29. okt. 1969) — de tastede \"LOGIN\", og forbindelsen brød sammen "
"efter to bogstaver.\n"
"tur-retur fuldført.\n"
"```"

#: src/getting-started.md:21
msgid ""
"`goat hello` publishes a message, subscribes to it, and watches it come back "
"— narrating every hop the data took. In the sandbox those hops are "
"simulated; against a real env they're real. Either way, when it says _round-"
"trip complete_, you know the path works end to end."
msgstr ""
"`goat hello` publicerer en besked, abonnerer på den og ser den komme tilbage "
"— mens den fortæller om hvert hop, dataene tog. I sandboxen er disse hop "
"simulerede; mod et rigtigt env er de ægte. Uanset hvad ved du, når den siger "
"_tur-retur fuldført_, at stien fungerer fra ende til ende."

#: src/getting-started.md:23
msgid ""
"The message is `lo` on purpose — the first thing ever sent over a network."
msgstr ""
"Beskeden er `lo` med vilje — det første, der nogensinde er sendt over et "
"netværk."

#: src/getting-started.md:25
msgid "2. Take the tour"
msgstr "2. Tag rundvisningen"

#: src/getting-started.md:31
msgid ""
"`goat tutor` is a self-paced, hands-on tour — think `vimtutor` for the "
"fabric. Eight short lessons take you from \"what is this\" to publishing, "
"subscribing, diagnosing, and reading the substrate cascade. It runs in the "
"sandbox by default, saves your place, and you can stop and resume any time:"
msgstr ""
"`goat tutor` er en selvstyret, praktisk rundvisning — tænk på `vimtutor` for "
"fabric. Otte korte lektioner tager dig fra \"hvad er dette\" til at "
"publicere, abonnere, diagnosticere og læse substratkaskaden. Den kører i "
"sandboxen som standard, gemmer dit sted, og du kan stoppe og genoptage når "
"som helst:"

#: src/getting-started.md:39
msgid "3. Attach a real environment"
msgstr "3. Tilknyt et rigtigt miljø"

#: src/getting-started.md:41
msgid ""
"When you've been issued an onboarding **bundle** (a `.cbor` file with your "
"identity), the wizard takes it from here:"
msgstr ""
"Når du er blevet udstedt et onboarding-**bundle** (en `.cbor`-fil med din "
"identitet), tager guiden over herfra:"

#: src/getting-started.md:49
msgid ""
"`goat init` is the friendly front door — it detects whether you're set up, "
"lets you choose the sandbox or a real env, proves it works, and points you "
"at the tutor. `goat doctor` then runs a stepped reachability check (mesh → "
"router → certificate → portal) and, if anything's wrong, tells you exactly "
"what to fix."
msgstr ""
"`goat init` er den venlige hoveddør — den registrerer, om du er sat op, "
"lader dig vælge sandboxen eller et rigtigt env, beviser at det virker, og "
"peger dig mod tutoren. `goat doctor` kører derefter et trinvist "
"tilgængelighedstjek (mesh → router → certifikat → portal) og fortæller dig, "
"hvis noget er galt, præcis hvad der skal rettes."

#: src/getting-started.md:51
msgid ""
"When all of doctor's steps pass, you'll see a small 🐐 — you're on the "
"fabric."
msgstr "Når alle doctors trin består, vil du se en lille 🐐 — du er på fabric."

#: src/getting-started.md:53
msgid "Where to next"
msgstr "Hvad nu"

#: src/getting-started.md:55
msgid "New to the ideas? Read **[How the fabric works](concepts.md)**."
msgstr "Ny til idéerne? Læs **[Sådan fungerer fabric](concepts.md)**."

#: src/getting-started.md:56
msgid "Ready to do things? Jump to **[Everyday tasks](everyday.md)**."
msgstr "Klar til at gøre ting? Hop til **[Daglige opgaver](everyday.md)**."

#: src/getting-started.md:57
msgid "Something not working? **[Troubleshooting](troubleshooting.md)**."
msgstr "Noget der ikke virker? **[Fejlfinding](troubleshooting.md)**."

#: src/concepts.md:3
msgid ""
"You can use goat productively with just three ideas: **identity**, "
"**topics**, and **no broker**. Here they are."
msgstr ""
"Du kan bruge goat produktivt med blot tre idéer: **identitet**, **topics** "
"og **ingen broker**. Her er de."

#: src/concepts.md:5
msgid "A mesh you join with an identity"
msgstr "Et mesh, du tilslutter dig med en identitet"

#: src/concepts.md:7
msgid ""
"The fabric is a self-healing mesh. Peers connect **directly** to each other "
"over encrypted WireGuard tunnels — once you're enrolled, your data doesn't "
"route through a central server, and your connections survive a management-"
"plane outage or a flaky uplink."
msgstr ""
"Fabric er et selvhelende mesh. Peers forbinder **direkte** til hinanden over "
"krypterede WireGuard-tunneler — når du er tilmeldt, routes dine data ikke "
"gennem en central server, og dine forbindelser overlever et nedbrud i "
"management-planet eller en ustabil uplink."

#: src/concepts.md:9
msgid ""
"You join with an **identity**: an onboarding _bundle_ that carries your "
"certificate, an access token, and where the fabric lives. The fabric admits "
"you by _who you are_, not by a shared password. `goat profile init "
"<bundle.cbor>` installs that identity; you can hold several under different "
"_contexts_ and switch between them."
msgstr ""
"Du tilslutter dig med en **identitet**: et onboarding-_bundle_, der bærer "
"dit certifikat, et adgangstoken og hvor fabric befinder sig. Fabric giver "
"dig adgang ud fra _hvem du er_, ikke ud fra en delt adgangskode. `goat "
"profile init <bundle.cbor>` installerer den identitet; du kan have flere "
"under forskellige _kontekster_ og skifte mellem dem."

#: src/concepts.md:19
msgid "Topics: publish and subscribe"
msgstr "Topics: publicér og abonnér"

#: src/concepts.md:21
msgid ""
"Data moves on **topics** — slash-delimited paths like `acme/radar1/tracks`. "
"The model is publish/subscribe:"
msgstr ""
"Data bevæger sig på **topics** — skråstregsadskilte stier som `acme/radar1/"
"tracks`. Modellen er publish/subscribe:"

#: src/concepts.md:23
msgid "**Publish** (`goat pub <topic> <payload>`) writes a value to a topic."
msgstr ""
"**Publish** (`goat pub <topic> <payload>`) skriver en værdi til et topic."

#: src/concepts.md:24
msgid ""
"**Subscribe** (`goat sub <topic>`) receives every value published there, "
"live, as long as you're allowed to read it."
msgstr ""
"**Subscribe** (`goat sub <topic>`) modtager hver værdi, der publiceres der, "
"live, så længe du har tilladelse til at læse det."

#: src/concepts.md:26
msgid ""
"A topic is just a name; you create it (`goat topic create`), publish to it, "
"and anyone permitted can subscribe. `goat hello` is simply a publish and a "
"subscribe wired together so you can watch a value make the round trip."
msgstr ""
"Et topic er bare et navn; du opretter det (`goat topic create`), publicerer "
"til det, og enhver med tilladelse kan abonnere. `goat hello` er ganske "
"enkelt en publish og en subscribe koblet sammen, så du kan se en værdi tage "
"turen frem og tilbage."

#: src/concepts.md:28
msgid "No broker — and why that matters"
msgstr "Ingen broker — og hvorfor det betyder noget"

#: src/concepts.md:30
msgid ""
"There is **no central broker** sitting in the middle of the data path. When "
"you publish, the value flows over the mesh directly to the peers subscribed "
"to it. That's deliberate: it removes the single bottleneck and single point "
"of failure that a broker would be."
msgstr ""
"Der er **ingen central broker**, der sidder i midten af datastien. Når du "
"publicerer, flyder værdien over mesh'et direkte til de peers, der abonnerer "
"på den. Det er bevidst: det fjerner den enkelte flaskehals og det enkelte "
"fejlpunkt, som en broker ville være."

#: src/concepts.md:32
msgid ""
"A practical consequence: **reads are broad, writes are the cut.** Being able "
"to _read_ a topic is permissive by design; _writing_ to one is governed by "
"your identity. So you'll rarely be surprised by what you can subscribe to, "
"and the integrity of what's published is anchored to who published it."
msgstr ""
"En praktisk konsekvens: **læsninger er brede, skrivninger er "
"afgrænsningen.** At kunne _læse_ et topic er tilladende efter design; at "
"_skrive_ til et styres af din identitet. Så du vil sjældent blive overrasket "
"over, hvad du kan abonnere på, og integriteten af det, der publiceres, er "
"forankret i, hvem der publicerede det."

#: src/concepts.md:34
msgid "Sandbox vs. real"
msgstr "Sandbox vs. ægte"

#: src/concepts.md:36
msgid ""
"Everything above has a faithful **in-process simulation** — the sandbox. "
"`goat hello --sandbox`, `goat init --sandbox`, and `goat tutor` exercise the "
"same shapes (a topic, a publish, a round-trip, a verdict) with no network "
"and no identity, so you can learn the model before you touch the real "
"fabric. The sandbox always says so with a `◇ SANDBOX` banner, and it never "
"writes to or reads from a real mesh."
msgstr ""
"Alt ovenstående har en trofast **in-process-simulation** — sandboxen. `goat "
"hello --sandbox`, `goat init --sandbox` og `goat tutor` øver de samme former "
"(et topic, en publish, en tur-retur, en kendelse) uden noget netværk og uden "
"nogen identitet, så du kan lære modellen, før du rører den rigtige fabric. "
"Sandboxen siger det altid med et `◇ SANDBOX`-banner, og den skriver aldrig "
"til eller læser fra et rigtigt mesh."

#: src/concepts.md:38
msgid ""
"When you switch to a real env, the _commands don't change_ — only the "
"backing does."
msgstr ""
"Når du skifter til et rigtigt env, ændrer _kommandoerne sig ikke_ — kun det "
"underliggende gør."

#: src/concepts.md:40
msgid ""
"Want the deeper architecture (the relay fallback, the access model, the "
"audit trail)? Ask your goat administrator for the design references — this "
"guide stays focused on operating the CLI."
msgstr ""
"Vil du have den dybere arkitektur (relay-fallback, adgangsmodellen, "
"revisionssporet)? Spørg din goat-administrator om designreferencerne — denne "
"guide holder fokus på at betjene CLI'en."

#: src/everyday.md:3
msgid ""
"The commands you'll actually reach for, as quick recipes. Add `--help` to "
"any of them for the full set of flags, or see the **[Command reference]"
"(reference.md)**."
msgstr ""
"De kommandoer, du faktisk vil bruge, som hurtige opskrifter. Tilføj `--help` "
"til en hvilken som helst af dem for det fulde sæt flag, eller se "
"**[Kommandoreference](reference.md)**."

#: src/everyday.md:5
msgid "Check you're connected"
msgstr "Tjek at du er forbundet"

#: src/everyday.md:12
msgid ""
"`goat doctor` is your first stop whenever something feels off — each step "
"that fails prints a specific remediation. When everything's green, both "
"commands give you a clear all-clear."
msgstr ""
"`goat doctor` er dit første stop, når noget føles galt — hvert trin, der "
"fejler, udskriver en specifik afhjælpning. Når alt er grønt, giver begge "
"kommandoer dig et tydeligt fri-skilt."

#: src/everyday.md:14
msgid "Publish and subscribe"
msgstr "Publicér og abonnér"

#: src/everyday.md:16
msgid ""
"```text\n"
"goat sub 'acme/radar1/tracks'             # watch a topic live (Ctrl-C to "
"stop)\n"
"goat sub 'acme/**'                        # a whole subtree\n"
"goat pub acme/radar1/tracks '{\"t\":1}'     # publish a payload\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```text\n"
"goat sub 'acme/radar1/tracks'             # se et topic live (Ctrl-C for at "
"stoppe)\n"
"goat sub 'acme/**'                        # et helt undertræ\n"
"goat pub acme/radar1/tracks '{\"t\":1}'     # publicér en payload\n"
"```"

#: src/everyday.md:22
msgid "Want to see the ripple a publish sets off? Add `--narrate`:"
msgstr "Vil du se den bølge, en publish udløser? Tilføj `--narrate`:"

#: src/everyday.md:24
msgid ""
"```text\n"
"goat pub acme/radar1/tracks '{\"t\":1}' --narrate\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```text\n"
"goat pub acme/radar1/tracks '{\"t\":1}' --narrate\n"
"```"

#: src/everyday.md:28
msgid "Work with topics"
msgstr "Arbejd med topics"

#: src/everyday.md:30
msgid ""
"```text\n"
"goat topic ls                              # list topics\n"
"goat topic ls acme                         # drill into an org/prefix\n"
"goat topic show acme/radar1/tracks         # one topic's full record\n"
"goat topic create acme/radar1/tracks --format protobuf:Track --description "
"\"live tracks\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```text\n"
"goat topic ls                              # vis topics\n"
"goat topic ls acme                         # bor ned i en organisation/et "
"præfiks\n"
"goat topic show acme/radar1/tracks         # ét topics fulde post\n"
"goat topic create acme/radar1/tracks --format protobuf:Track --description "
"\"live tracks\"\n"
"```"

#: src/everyday.md:37
msgid ""
"After you create a topic, goat nudges you toward the natural next step "
"(watch it, or publish to it)."
msgstr ""
"Når du har oprettet et topic, skubber goat dig mod det naturlige næste "
"skridt (se det eller publicér til det)."

#: src/everyday.md:39
msgid "Diagnose a problem"
msgstr "Diagnosticér et problem"

#: src/everyday.md:47
msgid ""
"`inspect` returns findings and the remedy for each — what's wrong and what "
"to do about it."
msgstr ""
"`inspect` returnerer fund og afhjælpningen for hvert — hvad der er galt, og "
"hvad man skal gøre ved det."

#: src/everyday.md:49
msgid "Scripting"
msgstr "Scripting"

#: src/everyday.md:51
msgid ""
"Every command that prints a human view also offers `--json` for a stable, "
"machine-readable one. The JSON form never carries banners, hints, or "
"flourishes, and its shape and your exit code stay constant across releases "
"and languages:"
msgstr ""
"Hver kommando, der udskriver en menneskelig visning, tilbyder også `--json` "
"for en stabil, maskinlæsbar en. JSON-formen bærer aldrig bannere, hints "
"eller udsmykninger, og dens form og din exit-kode forbliver konstante på "
"tværs af udgivelser og sprog:"

#: src/everyday.md:58
msgid "This is the contract: **friendly on a terminal, clean in a pipe.**"
msgstr "Dette er kontrakten: **venlig på en terminal, ren i en pipe.**"

#: src/everyday.md:60
msgid ""
"One caution: `goat status` opens a real session at the router each time it runs, so it is a check you run when you want an answer, not something to poll from a timer. For a trend over time use `goat health` or `goat top`, which read what the goatnet already publishes."
msgstr ""
"En advarsel: `goat status` åbner en rigtig session mod routeren, hver gang den kører, så det er et tjek, du kører, når du vil have et svar, ikke noget, der skal kaldes fra en timer. Til en tendens over tid skal du bruge `goat health` eller `goat top`, som læser det, goatnet allerede udgiver."

#: src/install.md:3
msgid ""
"goat is a single self-contained binary — no runtime, no dependencies. It's "
"served mesh-internally from `get.<your-goatnet>` (you're already on the mesh "
"if you can read this), and the version here always matches the binary that "
"surface serves."
msgstr ""
"goat er en enkelt selvstændig binær — ingen runtime, ingen afhængigheder. "
"Den serveres mesh-internt fra `get.<your-goatnet>` (du er allerede på "
"mesh'et, hvis du kan læse dette), og versionen her matcher altid den binær, "
"som den overflade serverer."

#: src/install.md:5
msgid "Quick install"
msgstr "Hurtig installation"

#: src/install.md:7
msgid "**macOS / Linux**"
msgstr "**macOS / Linux**"

#: src/install.md:10
msgid ""
"$(uname -s | tr '[:upper:]' '[:lower:]')              # darwin | linux\n"
msgstr ""
"$(uname -s | tr '[:upper:]' '[:lower:]')              # darwin | linux\n"

#: src/install.md:11
msgid "$(uname -m | sed 's/x86_64/amd64/;s/aarch64/arm64/')  # amd64 | arm64\n"
msgstr ""
"$(uname -m | sed 's/x86_64/amd64/;s/aarch64/arm64/')  # amd64 | arm64\n"

#: src/install.md:12
msgid "\"https://get.<your-goatnet>/goat-${OS}-${ARCH}\""
msgstr "\"https://get.<your-goatnet>/goat-${OS}-${ARCH}\""

#: src/install.md:17
msgid "Make sure `~/.local/bin` is on your `PATH`."
msgstr "Sørg for, at `~/.local/bin` er på din `PATH`."

#: src/install.md:19
msgid "**Windows (PowerShell)**"
msgstr "**Windows (PowerShell)**"

#: src/install.md:21
msgid ""
"```powershell\n"
"iwr \"https://get.<your-goatnet>/goat-windows-amd64.exe\" -OutFile "
"\"$env:USERPROFILE\\goat.exe\"\n"
"& \"$env:USERPROFILE\\goat.exe\" --version\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```powershell\n"
"iwr \"https://get.<your-goatnet>/goat-windows-amd64.exe\" -OutFile "
"\"$env:USERPROFILE\\goat.exe\"\n"
"& \"$env:USERPROFILE\\goat.exe\" --version\n"
"```"

#: src/install.md:26
msgid ""
"Every subcommand works on Windows except `goat client` (the local tunnel "
"daemon), which is Linux/macOS-only."
msgstr ""
"Hver underkommando fungerer på Windows undtagen `goat client` (den lokale "
"tunnel-daemon), som kun er til Linux/macOS."

#: src/install.md:28
msgid "Verify the download (recommended)"
msgstr "Verificér downloaden (anbefalet)"

#: src/install.md:30
msgid ""
"The download surface publishes a per-binary `*.sha256` and an aggregate "
"`SHA256SUMS`. For a high-assurance install, verify before you run:"
msgstr ""
"Download-overfladen publicerer en `*.sha256` pr. binær og en samlet "
"`SHA256SUMS`. For en installation med høj sikkerhed skal du verificere, før "
"du kører:"

#: src/install.md:33
